  "body": "**Status: research note with exact finite computations and written proofs (not a SAT/DRAT proof). No \u03ba claim, no supplier word.** Only `research/one-sided-decoders-all-m/` is added; nothing existing is changed.\n\n## What this proves (scope is the claim)\n\nModel of #2338 / #2277 / #2724 / #1224: exact masked decoders `N = \u03a3_{j\u2264m} p_j q_j\u1d40` of the **Gram realisation** of the P112 pattern, field of **characteristic 0**, dense pairing table `B`, cost `\u03a3_j rank_F2 B[R_j, A_j]`. **Case (b): one factor outside `col M`** (the other in `col M`), **every number of terms `m`**. Reduced to the `(y, U)` form; the decoder is a lift `S \u2287 \ud835\udc9e` of the root code, `cost \u2265 cost_w(S)` (min-weight basis).\n\n* **R1 (CHECKED + PROVEN).** \u03b5-free one-sided P112 decoders cost **\u2265 64 for every `d = dim(\ud835\udc9e \u2229 S_{\u22647})`**: exact DP for `d \u2264 6`, an LP with exact integer dual certificates for `d = 7, 8` (`lp3.py`), re-derived by an independent symmetrised LP with exact rational duals (`symlp.py`); the multiset enumeration is complete (`enum.py`: none for `d \u2264 6`, one at `d = 7`, seven at `d = 8`, all killed).\n* **R2 (Theorem U\u2032).** The cost-64 \u03b5-free decoder is **unique**: the coordinate decoder (8 terms `(e_j, W_j)`). Cost-65 decoders have at most one non-full correction; the cost-66 case is reduced to six OPEN `d = 8` weight multisets.\n* **R3 (corrections).** Lemma P: a *full* corrected term (`U = F2\u2079`) is absorbed at no cost. **Corrected cost \u2265 64 whenever at most 2 corrected terms of the normalised decoder are non-full** (normalise = merge proportional corrected terms and absorb full ones, repeated until stable; terminates since (#terms, #full corrected) drops lexicographically; the version for raw decoders is the lift-level form R4 with `I` = all corrected terms); in general `\u2265 64 \u2212 max(0, n_nf \u2212 2) \u2265 58`. The **root-swap family attains 64 exactly** with `n_nf = 1, 2, 3, 4` (exact `P\u00b7Y = C`), so `\u0394 \u2265 n_nf` is tight.\n* **R4 (lift level).** Every `S \u2287 \ud835\udc9e_{X_I}` has `cost_w(S) \u2265 64 + min(|I|, 2)`; every lift of the E8 root code has `cost_w \u2265 66`.\n* **R5.** Lemma N (\u2264 2 directions per 7-flat after removing \u2264 4 lines; exact counts for `|L| = 1, 2`, an upper bound for `|L| \u2264 4`, and an independent C implementation) and the Pencil Lemma (`d \u2264 2`).\n* Gain-law reading (philippeVV, Discussion #1587 follow-up 6): in this class the gain on P112 is at most 48 (`112 \u2212 64`).\n\n## Open residue (stated exactly, not claimed)\n\n`\u0394 \u2265 n_nf` for `n_nf \u2265 3`: at `n_nf = 3` exactly six `d = 8` multisets of the weight-\u22647 basis remain (`[7^5,6^5,1]`, `[7^6,6^4]`, `[7^8,5,4,1]`, `[7^8,5,5]`, `[7^8,6,3,1]`, `[7^8,6,4]`). Not claimed here.\n\n## Not covered (stated up front)\n\n* Case (c) (rank-9 realisations, see #2784), two-sided decoders, P104 and other units, `B` of rank \u2265 10, positive characteristic.\n* **Imported (merged results, not re-derived):** Gram realisation (#1212 Theorem 1, plus a diagonal normalisation); dense table (#2338 Theorem R, DRAT-checked there). The parabolic-flat fact is proved in the README (C3).\n* Not DRAT / Lean: written proofs plus exact Python/C computations, re-runnable.\n\n## Labels and verification\n\nPROVEN / CHECKED / RECORDED / IMPORTED / OPEN per claim in the README. `bash verify.sh` (about 12\u201315 minutes, two processes, no SAT) re-runs every exact check (DP, enumeration, LP certificates, Lemma N in two implementations, the root-swap family) and asserts them in `checks/check_logs.py`; fresh `git archive` export: 34 PASS / 0 FAIL in 714 s (logs in `evidence/logs`).\n\n## Overlap\n\nScanned the 1,000 most recent PRs (titles), 119 decoder-related bodies and 100 recent Discussions: no \u03b5-free one-sided floor for all `m`, LP/charging certificates, uniqueness statement, root-swap family or Lemma N. Nearest: #1224 (model), #1180 (both factors in the root code), #1633, #1815, #1609, and our #2338 / #2277 / #2724 (this is the every-`m` extension of #2724's case (b) at `m = 9`, by a different method).\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
